From: Dynabook investigation <root@local>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: toshiba_acpi: drain INFO FIFO on each hotkey Notify

On Dynabook Portege X40-K (ACPI id "DNBK0001", a rebranded Toshiba),
the EC enqueues a press entry (0x14x) and a companion/release entry
(0x1Cx) into the AFIF ring for every physical hotkey, and may coalesce
multiple keys into fewer SCI Notify events.

toshiba_acpi_process_hotkeys() reads the INFO method only ONCE per
Notify when info_supported is set, then returns. This leaves stale
entries in the ring that are replayed on a later keypress, causing
hotkey functions to "bleed" into one another / persist across presses
(e.g. pressing brightness-up is interpreted as brightness-down for the
next 2-3 presses).

Fix by draining the entire FIFO on each Notify (loop until INFO returns
0), mirroring the existing HCI_SYSTEM_EVENT path which already loops
until TOS_FIFO_EMPTY.

Signed-off-by: Dynabook investigation <root@local>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/toshiba_acpi.c
@@ -2822,10 +2822,20 @@ static void toshiba_acpi_process_hotkeys(struct toshiba_acpi_dev *dev)
 {
 	if (dev->info_supported) {
-		int scancode = toshiba_acpi_query_hotkey(dev);
-
-		if (scancode < 0) {
-			pr_err("Failed to query hotkey event\n");
-		} else if (scancode != 0) {
+		/*
+		 * Drain the entire INFO FIFO on each SCI Notify. The EC may
+		 * enqueue a press (0x14x) and a companion/release (0x1Cx)
+		 * entry per physical key, and may coalesce multiple keys
+		 * into fewer Notify events. Reading only one entry per
+		 * Notify leaves stale entries in the ring that get replayed
+		 * on a later keypress (key functions "bleeding" into each
+		 * other / persisting across presses). Loop until INFO
+		 * returns 0 (ring empty), matching the HCI_SYSTEM_EVENT
+		 * path's TOS_FIFO_EMPTY drain semantics.
+		 */
+		for (;;) {
+			int scancode = toshiba_acpi_query_hotkey(dev);
+
+			if (scancode < 0) {
+				pr_err("Failed to query hotkey event\n");
+				break;
+			}
+			if (scancode == 0)
+				break;	/* FIFO empty */
+
 			toshiba_acpi_report_hotkey(dev, scancode);
 			dev->key_event_valid = 1;
 			dev->last_key_event = scancode;
-- 
